  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a completed `npm install`, when `npm run typecheck` is run in src/client/office-addins and the output is filtered to paths under word/ and outlook/, then zero errors are reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same typecheck run, when the per-directory counts for shared/taskpane/, shared/adapters/, shared/services/ and shared/__mocks__/ are compared against the task 001 baseline, then none has increased.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` exits 0 and both the Word and Outlook bundles emit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm test` exits 0 with suite and test counts greater than or equal to the task 001 baseline — no test was deleted, skipped or replaced with a weaker assertion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: src/client/office-addins/word/WordHostAdapter.ts still exists, and `git diff` on it shows no change to the semantics of `getCompressedFile()` — no altered Office.js call, no changed slicing or encoding, no changed error path (plan.md finding F-e; task 010 ports it verbatim).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff` shows no change to any ribbon command's registered name or signature in word/commands/index.ts or outlook/commands/index.ts, and neither `quickSave` nor `shareDocument` was implemented or removed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff --name-only` lists no manifest or html file — specifically not word/word-manifest.xml, outlook/manifest.json, outlook/outlook-manifest.xml, or any taskpane.html / commands.html — and no version string was bumped.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `grep` across the diff finds no newly added `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `grep` across the diff finds no `Xrm` reference (NFR-03), no `new PublicClientApplication`, no `createNestablePublicClientApplication`, no `.WithClientSecret`, and no new import from `@azure/msal-browser` (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff` shows src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json, package.json and package-lock.json unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff --name-only` lists no file under shared/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no import from `@spaarke/ui-components` was added (ADR-012 Path A exception, NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All four ui-tests below pass in both hosts and their results are recorded, including the dark-mode check in both directions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md contains a section headed for task 008 recording the fix shapes used and confirming word/WordHostAdapter.ts survives with unchanged `getCompressedFile()` semantics.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Step 9.5 code-review and adr-check gates ran and their findings are resolved or explicitly accepted.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec reference: FR-18 (line 92), FR-04 (line 64), FR-05 (line 65), FR-17 (line 91), NFR-03 (line 100), Success Criterion 12 (line 209). Plan reference: section 4 Phase 0 tasks 006-008, finding F-e, Phase 1 tasks 010 and 011, Phase 3 task 037.

No `&lt;justification&gt;` block is present: this is a modify-only task. It adds no new service, abstraction, endpoint, DI registration, package or column — CLAUDE.md section 11's gate does not apply to edits of existing files.

Parallel-safety within the P0-typecheck wave: 006 owns shared/taskpane/**, 007 owns shared/adapters/** plus shared/services/** (plus shared/__mocks__/** conditionally), 008 owns word/** plus outlook/**. The three directory sets are disjoint. The shared surfaces are node_modules (read-only concurrency, fine) and projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md — task 006 creates it and 007/008 append clearly headed sections, so keep edits additive and scoped to your own heading. tsconfig.json is out of scope for all three, which removes the one file they would otherwise contend for.

Sizing note: word/ contained 3 .ts/.tsx files and outlook/ 3 at authoring time — the smallest bucket. The task 001 rollup, not this note, is the authority on the error count. If the measured error count for these six files is large relative to their size, WordHostAdapter.ts is the likely concentration; keep its diff minimal regardless, since task 010 deletes it.

Downstream: task 010 (FR-04, prescriptive — ports `getCompressedFile()` then deletes word/WordHostAdapter.ts), task 011 (FR-05 Word unified JSON manifest), task 037 (FR-17 ribbon commands) and task 042 (deploy) all build on this directory pair. Leaving it compiling and otherwise untouched is the deliverable.</notes>

